@(14 = 14-15) I am a scribe and I write on stelae. @vart[t3121.v13,t3121.v13]{@varn{2 ms. add:} …… business concerning the troops. } I will …… business which has been neglected in the assembly, when it ……. @vart[t3121.v14,t3121.v14]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} …… business which makes good …… equal. }

@(16 = 16-19) But like a tree planted in riverine thickets, I am bowed down in dirt. They have bound a rope around my hands, on my chair where they have tied me. In my city, where I would wear clean clothes, I am clothed instead in mourning dress. When I wash away clods of soil, dust still gets into my eyes.

@(20 = 20-23) Dogs devour corpses, lifting their chests. When dragons kill, what is left from their mouths is put aside. Fire consumes reedbeds even though they have waterways. @wDN{Utu}, who eats butter, who eats cream, nevertheless touches the table of the poor. @vart[t3121.v15,t3121.v15]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} Grant me my life and hold my hands! I am a son of a widow, and I have no one to take care of me. }

@(24 = 24) As for me, when will the heart of @wRN{Šulgi}, my lord, be restored to me? @vart[t3121.v16,t3121.v16]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} May my lord attend to me and restore me to my mother. }



